Subject: [PATCH 11104/11362] [outer-loop] Correct the GPU claim and record
 that eval artifacts carry no hardware provenance

Correction 3, promised last hour. The r11l eval was reported as GPU 1 only
and is on both cards: its llama-server holds 10.5 GB on GPU 0 and 11.4 GB on
GPU 1. CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU selects a preferred device and does not
mask the others. The split is required rather than wrong, because the 27B at
n_ctx 98304 exceeds one 24 GB card, so confining it means lowering n_ctx and
losing comparability with the control. The run stays on both cards and the
allocation conflict is now stated in the record instead of in chat.

Second occurrence this session; the first was bd08d8d071. Prose did not stop
the repeat, so the GPU-pinning memory now carries the settling command rather
than the intention: read placement from nvidia-smi compute-apps joined to the
uuid map, never from the environment you set.

Measured separately: 13 of 13 eval run artifacts record no GPU, VRAM, n_ctx,
device or model-server field. The n_ctx conclusion, the decode rate and the
engine table all rest on runs whose artifacts cannot state what produced
them. That is a G2 reproducibility gap, not a cosmetic one.

